necessarily better looking.

00:02:08.435 --> 00:02:10.679
I think, for me, it's just strange.

00:02:10.679 --> 00:02:13.345
(light orchestra music)

00:02:15.545 --> 00:02:16.788
- Glue?

00:02:16.788 --> 00:02:18.228
You want me to put glue on my eye?

00:02:18.228 --> 00:02:20.558
If this gets in my eye, will I go blind?

00:02:20.558 --> 00:02:21.723
- [Voiceover] No.

00:02:21.723 --> 00:02:22.291
- Alright, let's do it.

00:02:22.291 --> 00:02:24.381
- This is the product that
I used in high school,

00:02:24.381 --> 00:02:26.308
and if I remember correctly,

00:02:26.308 --> 00:02:28.247
I needed to use, like, a lot of glue.

00:02:28.247 --> 00:02:29.745
- This some horror movie shit right here.

00:02:29.745 --> 00:02:32.497
- It's so much easier to just
love what your mama gave you.

00:02:32.497 --> 00:02:35.381
- Oh no, that's terrifying.

00:02:35.381 --> 00:02:37.355
- [Voiceover] Oh shit.

00:02:37.355 --> 00:02:39.259
- This is it, it stuck.

00:02:39.259 --> 00:02:40.350
That took like two seconds.

00:02:40.350 --> 00:02:42.000
- You know what, what a world we live in,

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:44.322
where you can alter the shape of your face

00:02:44.322 --> 00:02:45.633
how ever you want to.

00:02:45.633 --> 00:02:46.898
- As soon as I put it on, I'm just like,

00:02:46.898 --> 00:02:49.696
"Oh yeah, like, I
remember why I used that."

00:02:49.696 --> 00:02:50.915
And it's like, I don't think anyone else

00:02:50.915 --> 00:02:53.401
would notice the difference
in my face, except for me.

00:02:53.401 --> 00:02:55.523
(light violin music)

00:02:56.814 --> 00:02:58.138
- This freaked me out.

00:02:58.138 --> 00:02:59.300
This really freaked me out.

00:02:59.300 --> 00:03:01.354
Cause I don't even recognize

00:03:01.354 --> 00:03:02.934
the person I'm looking at in this mirror.

00:03:02.934 --> 00:03:05.000
- I feel like I'm more
accepting of my monolids,

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:06.300
because this just made me realize

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:09.434
how much I don't care about
having double eyelids.

00:03:09.434 --> 00:03:11.291
- I started using these
products when I was younger,

00:03:11.291 --> 00:03:13.034
and I was a lot more insecure.

00:03:13.034 --> 00:03:14.299
And now that I'm an adult,

00:03:14.299 --> 00:03:16.933
I think I should probably be
at this place where it's like,

00:03:16.933 --> 00:03:18.734
"Oh yeah, like, I'm totally cool,

00:03:18.734 --> 00:03:21.229
and I don't feel insecure
about my eyes anymore."

00:03:21.229 --> 00:03:23.956
And it's like, obviously
that's not totally true.

00:03:23.956 --> 00:03:26.372
- I'm wondering if it
would've been worth, like,

00:03:26.372 --> 00:03:29.135
getting the double eyelid
surgery when I was younger.

00:03:29.135 --> 00:03:32.885
And I don't think so, cause I
like my eyes the way they are.

00:03:32.885 --> 00:03:36.591
- For those who are
struggling with their looks,

00:03:36.591 --> 00:03:38.263
